/T (@ManyToMany maps a relationship where many records on one side can be associated with many records on the other side. Example: one Customer can have many Offers, and one Offer can be shared by many Customers. Because no single table can hold a foreign key for both sides, a separate join table is created.)
/E (@ManyToMany maps a relationship where many records on one side can be associated with many records on the other side. Example: one Customer can have many Offers, and one Offer can be shared by many Customers. Because no single table can hold a foreign key for both sides, a separate join table is created.)
